## Key Implementation Decisions

### Plugin Registration Strategy
Chose to register both WebSocket and store plugins to maintain full functionality from both branches:
```rust
.plugin(tauri_plugin_websocket::init())
.plugin(tauri_plugin_store::Builder::default().build())
```

### State Management Integration
Integrated cloud fields into main AppState structure rather than creating separate state management:
```rust
pub cloud_client: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<CloudClient>>>,
pub cloud_config: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<CloudConfig>>>,
pub cloud_enabled: Arc<Mutex<bool>>,
pub production_cloud_connector: Arc<TokioMutex<Option<ProductionCloudConnector>>>,
```

### Command Handler Consolidation
Preserved all command handlers from both branches in a single invoke handler:
```rust
.invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![
    // Original commands preserved
    // Keyboard shortcut commands preserved
    // Cloud commands added
])
```

